course: dictionary
lesson: 13963
title: Limitation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A limitation is something that stops a person or thing from doing everything it might want to do. «The robot has some limitations: it can climb stairs but it cannot swim.» The clues are "some limitations" and "cannot swim", so a limitation is something that holds back what the robot can do.
explain: The word limit is a useful clue. A limitation is about a limit, the edge where something stops. Limitations can be things a person or machine cannot do, or they can be about time or money, such as «time limitations» when you do not have long enough to finish a task.
explain: In science, the limitations of an experiment are its weak points, the things that could make the results less accurate. «Our study had only ten children, which is a limitation.» Good scientists name their limitations honestly, so that other people know how far to trust the results.
explain: Knowing your limitations means being honest about what you can and cannot do well. Ask yourself: what can I not do yet, and what is my limit? Saying so is sensible, not a failure.
fact: A limitation is something that limits what a person or thing can do.
fact: «Know your limitations» means know what you can and cannot do well.
fact: In science, the limitations of an experiment are its weaknesses, things that could make the results less accurate.
fact: Limitation can also mean keeping something under control or within limits, as in «the limitation of noise».
fact: Other phrases you will meet are «limitations of the study» and «time limitations».
exercise: «The robot has some limitations.» What does limitations mean here? | Friends who help the robot | Lights that show the robot is switched on | *Things that limit what the robot can do | Parts that make the robot faster
exercise: Scientists write the limitations of their experiment. What are they? | Its long and difficult title | Its best results, which are always perfect | *Its weaknesses, things that could make the results less accurate | Its colours and pictures
exercise: Which phrase means knowing what you can and cannot do well? | Know your favourite colour | *Know your limitations | Know the way to the shops | Know your neighbours
test: «We had time limitations, so we could only test five plants.» What does time limitations suggest? | *Not enough time to do everything | Far too much time to finish | Time spent travelling to the moon | A clock that has been broken
test: Which sentence uses limitation the way a science report would? | *The small sample size is a limitation of our study | The sun is a limitation of our study | Limitation is my favourite word in the whole book | We painted a limitation on the poster
exam: Ella says a limitation is a prize for good work. Is she right? | No, a limitation is a type of food | Yes, a limitation is a kind of party | *No, a limitation is something that limits what a person or thing can do | Yes, a limitation is a prize given to the best pupil
